Changed: IBAMR::StaggeredStokesFACPreconditionerStrategy overrides IBTK::FACPreconditionerStrategy::reinitializeOperatorState(). IBAMR::StaggeredStokesBoxRelaxationFACOperator and IBAMR::StaggeredStokesLevelRelaxationFACOperator reuse their layout when the hierarchy, the vectors, and getLayoutKeySpecialized() are unchanged. In that case, they call initializeOperatorCoefficientsSpecialized() instead of initializeOperatorStateSpecialized(). A subclass of one of these operators must follow the rule for subclasses of the Poisson FAC operators: if its initializeOperatorStateSpecialized() override, or the state that its smoothError() or computeResidual() override reads, depends on the coefficients or the boundary conditions, it must either override initializeOperatorCoefficientsSpecialized() and call the base function, or override getLayoutKeySpecialized() to return false. Direct subclasses of IBAMR::StaggeredStokesFACPreconditionerStrategy, and IBAMR::StaggeredStokesIBLevelRelaxationFACOperator, see no change. The two operators now re-initialize their coarse and level solvers without deallocating them, which relies on the contract of IBTK::GeneralSolver::initializeSolverState(). The new overrides change the vtables of these classes.
